BEGIN_TEXT
Every ALE transmission the radio has decoded, newest first: when, on
which channel, who called (the caller), who was called, what kind it was,
and how clean it was (SINAD, in dB: higher is cleaner).

A sounding is a station saying "I am here" to no one in particular. A call
names the station it wants. A call-end closes a link. Short messages sent
inside a call (AMD) are shown with it.

A call to your own address heard in the last minute shows at the top as
INCOMING. Your own address comes with the box (own_address.txt); it isn't
typed here.

Words marked with lost samples were decoded across a gap in what the radio
heard: their calls may be incomplete.
END
